Notebook[{
Cell[TextData[{
  "Week 9   Projective Geometry\n",
  StyleBox["Extra Material on ",
    FontSize->18],
  StyleBox["n",
    FontSize->18,
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  StyleBox["th Powers",
    FontSize->18]
}], "Title"],

Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Copyright] Dana Scott 1993/1997/1998",
    FontSize->16,
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  StyleBox["\nNotebook  last edited: ",
    FontSize->16],
  StyleBox["22 October 1998",
    FontSize->16,
    FontWeight->"Bold"]
}], "Subtitle",
  FontSize->18],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Three cubes", "Subsubsection"],

Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["Problem.  ",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "To show ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox[\(x\ y\ z\),
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  " is ",
  StyleBox["not",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " the sum of three cubes of linear polynomials."
}], "Text",
  Background->RGBColor[0, 1, 1]],

Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["Solution.  ",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "Suppose we could write ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox[\(x\ y\ z\  == \ l\^3 + m\^3 + n\^3\),
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  ".  Note that ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox[\(x\ y\ z\),
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  " has three ",
  StyleBox["double points",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  ":"
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\(PD[x\ y\ z, #\^2]&\)\ /@\ {u, v, w}\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \({0, 0, 0}\)], "Output"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[TextData[{
  "But \[LongDash] as we already know in any case \[LongDash] it has no ",
  StyleBox["triple point",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  ":"
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(Tidy[PD[x\ y\ z, a\ u + b\ v + c\ w]]\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(c\ x\ y + b\ x\ z + a\ y\ z\)], "Output"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Now, if ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox[\(x\ y\ z\),
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  " ",
  StyleBox["is",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " the sum of three cubes of linear polynomials, they cannot reduce to all \
multiples of the ",
  StyleBox["same",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " linear polynomial, because a curve such as ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox[\(l\^3\),
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  " has ",
  StyleBox["only",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  StyleBox[" ",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "triple points."
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Soi if the lines ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox["l",
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  ", ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox["m",
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  " , and ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox["n",
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  " are ",
  StyleBox["independent",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  ", then we can transform them to ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox["x",
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  ", ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox["y",
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  ", ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox["z",
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  " by a projective transformation.  But, their cubic sum has ",
  StyleBox["no",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " ",
  StyleBox["double point",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " at all."
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(PD[x\^3 + y\^3 + z\^3, \((a\ u + b\ v + c\ w)\)\^2] // Tidy\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(6\ a\^2\ x + 6\ b\^2\ y + 6\ c\^2\ z\)], "Output"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Therefore that case is impossible.  If, on the other hand, the lines are ",
  
  StyleBox["dependent",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  ", then \[LongDash] after a suitable transformation to ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox["x",
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  ", ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox["y",
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  " , and ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox[\(\[Lambda]\ x + \[Mu]\ y\),
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  " \[LongDash] we see the sum has a triple point. "
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(PD[x\^3 + y\^3 + \((\[Lambda]\ x + \[Mu]\ y)\)\^3, w] // Tidy\)], 
  "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(0\)], "Output"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[TextData[{
  "However, the \"curve\" ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox[\(x\ y\ z\),
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  " \[LongDash] after ",
  StyleBox["every",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " projective transformation \[LongDash] has ",
  StyleBox["3 ",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "double points but ",
  StyleBox["no",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " triple point.  Hence,  ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox[\(x\ y\ z\),
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  " is not a sum of three cubes. ",
  StyleBox["Q.E.D.",
    FontWeight->"Bold"]
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["Comment.",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "  Note that we have shown by this method that the cubic polynomial\n\t\t\t\
",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox[\(x\^3 + y\^3 + \((\[Lambda]\ x + \[Mu]\ y)\)\^3\),
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  "  \n",
  StyleBox["always factors",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " into linear factors.  ",
  StyleBox["However, we already knew that homogeneous polynomials in ",
    FontWeight->"Plain"],
  StyleBox["two variables",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  StyleBox[" always factor!  ",
    FontWeight->"Plain"]
}], "Text",
  Background->RGBColor[0, 1, 0]],

Cell[TextData[{
  "To factor, we just have to solve the equation for ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox[\(t == x/y\),
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  " in the usual way."
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    RowBox[{"Solve", "[", 
      StyleBox[
        RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
            RowBox[{\(t\^3\), "+", \(1\^3\), "+", 
              SuperscriptBox[
                RowBox[{"(", 
                  RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", 
                      StyleBox["t",
                        FontWeight->"Bold"]}], "+", 
                    RowBox[{"\[Mu]", " ", 
                      StyleBox["1",
                        FontWeight->"Bold"]}]}], ")"}], "3"]}], "==", "0"}], 
          ",", \({t}\)}],
        FontWeight->"Bold"], 
      StyleBox["]",
        FontWeight->"Bold"]}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \({{t \[Rule] 
          \(-\(\(\[Lambda]\^2\ \[Mu]\)\/\(1 + \[Lambda]\^3\)\)\) - 
            \((3\ 2\^\(1/3\)\ \[Lambda]\ \[Mu]\^2)\)/
              \((\((1 + \[Lambda]\^3)\)\ 
                  \((\(-54\)\ \[Lambda]\^6\ \[Mu]\^3 + 
                        81\ \[Lambda]\^3\ \((1 + \[Lambda]\^3)\)\ \[Mu]\^3 - 
                        27\ \((1 + \[Lambda]\^3)\)\^2\ \((1 + \[Mu]\^3)\) + 
                        27\ \((1 + \[Lambda]\^3)\)\ 
                          \@\(1 + 2\ \[Lambda]\^3 + \[Lambda]\^6 + 
                              2\ \[Mu]\^3 - 2\ \[Lambda]\^3\ \[Mu]\^3 + 
                              \[Mu]\^6\))\)^\((1/3)\))\) + 
            \((\(-54\)\ \[Lambda]\^6\ \[Mu]\^3 + 
                    81\ \[Lambda]\^3\ \((1 + \[Lambda]\^3)\)\ \[Mu]\^3 - 
                    27\ \((1 + \[Lambda]\^3)\)\^2\ \((1 + \[Mu]\^3)\) + 
                    27\ \((1 + \[Lambda]\^3)\)\ 
                      \@\(1 + 2\ \[Lambda]\^3 + \[Lambda]\^6 + 2\ \[Mu]\^3 - 
                          2\ \[Lambda]\^3\ \[Mu]\^3 + \[Mu]\^6\))\)^\((1/3)\)/
              \((3\ 2\^\(1/3\)\ \((1 + \[Lambda]\^3)\))\)}, {
        t \[Rule] 
          \(-\(\(\[Lambda]\^2\ \[Mu]\)\/\(1 + \[Lambda]\^3\)\)\) + 
            \((3\ \((1 + I\ \@3)\)\ \[Lambda]\ \[Mu]\^2)\)/
              \((2\^\(2/3\)\ \((1 + \[Lambda]\^3)\)\ 
                  \((\(-54\)\ \[Lambda]\^6\ \[Mu]\^3 + 
                        81\ \[Lambda]\^3\ \((1 + \[Lambda]\^3)\)\ \[Mu]\^3 - 
                        27\ \((1 + \[Lambda]\^3)\)\^2\ \((1 + \[Mu]\^3)\) + 
                        27\ \((1 + \[Lambda]\^3)\)\ 
                          \@\(1 + 2\ \[Lambda]\^3 + \[Lambda]\^6 + 
                              2\ \[Mu]\^3 - 2\ \[Lambda]\^3\ \[Mu]\^3 + 
                              \[Mu]\^6\))\)^\((1/3)\))\) - 
            \((\((1 - I\ \@3)\)\ 
                  \((\(-54\)\ \[Lambda]\^6\ \[Mu]\^3 + 
                        81\ \[Lambda]\^3\ \((1 + \[Lambda]\^3)\)\ \[Mu]\^3 - 
                        27\ \((1 + \[Lambda]\^3)\)\^2\ \((1 + \[Mu]\^3)\) + 
                        27\ \((1 + \[Lambda]\^3)\)\ 
                          \@\(1 + 2\ \[Lambda]\^3 + \[Lambda]\^6 + 
                              2\ \[Mu]\^3 - 2\ \[Lambda]\^3\ \[Mu]\^3 + 
                              \[Mu]\^6\))\)^\((1/3)\))\)/
              \((6\ 2\^\(1/3\)\ \((1 + \[Lambda]\^3)\))\)}, {
        t \[Rule] 
          \(-\(\(\[Lambda]\^2\ \[Mu]\)\/\(1 + \[Lambda]\^3\)\)\) + 
            \((3\ \((1 - I\ \@3)\)\ \[Lambda]\ \[Mu]\^2)\)/
              \((2\^\(2/3\)\ \((1 + \[Lambda]\^3)\)\ 
                  \((\(-54\)\ \[Lambda]\^6\ \[Mu]\^3 + 
                        81\ \[Lambda]\^3\ \((1 + \[Lambda]\^3)\)\ \[Mu]\^3 - 
                        27\ \((1 + \[Lambda]\^3)\)\^2\ \((1 + \[Mu]\^3)\) + 
                        27\ \((1 + \[Lambda]\^3)\)\ 
                          \@\(1 + 2\ \[Lambda]\^3 + \[Lambda]\^6 + 
                              2\ \[Mu]\^3 - 2\ \[Lambda]\^3\ \[Mu]\^3 + 
                              \[Mu]\^6\))\)^\((1/3)\))\) - 
            \((\((1 + I\ \@3)\)\ 
                  \((\(-54\)\ \[Lambda]\^6\ \[Mu]\^3 + 
                        81\ \[Lambda]\^3\ \((1 + \[Lambda]\^3)\)\ \[Mu]\^3 - 
                        27\ \((1 + \[Lambda]\^3)\)\^2\ \((1 + \[Mu]\^3)\) + 
                        27\ \((1 + \[Lambda]\^3)\)\ 
                          \@\(1 + 2\ \[Lambda]\^3 + \[Lambda]\^6 + 
                              2\ \[Mu]\^3 - 2\ \[Lambda]\^3\ \[Mu]\^3 + 
                              \[Mu]\^6\))\)^\((1/3)\))\)/
              \((6\ 2\^\(1/3\)\ \((1 + \[Lambda]\^3)\))\)}}\)], "Output"]
}, Closed]],

Cell["\<\
Ugh, the roots are not much fun to look at.  But there you \
are!\
\>", "Text"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Many powers", "Subsubsection"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Marko Petkovsek (a former CMU student), found the \"triangular\" \
configuration showing how to get one maximal independent set of ",
  StyleBox["n",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  "th powers.  He then converted this insight into a (somewhat long) program \
for ",
  StyleBox["finding",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " a representation of any monomial as a linear combination of powers.  Here \
is the program (fortunately made to work again by Aleks Nanevski):"
}], "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[{
    \(\(BeginPackage["\<Monomials`\>"]; \)\), 
    \(\(GeneratePartition::"\<usage\>" = 
      "\<GeneratePartition[n, v] generates all ordered partitions of n into v \
parts.\>"; \)\), 
    \(\(Convert::"\<usage\>" = 
      "\<Convert[mon, Start -> s, Step -> h] expresses monomial mon of degree \
n as a linear combination of n-th powers of linear forms. The optional \
parameters affect the choice of  coefficients in these forms.\>"; \)\), 
    \(\(ConvertAll::"\<usage\>" = 
      "\<ConvertAll[n, v, Start -> s, Step -> h,  Vars -> {x,y,z,..}] \
expresses all monomials of degree n as linear  combinations of n-th powers of \
linear forms. The optional parameters  affect the choice of coefficients and \
variables in these forms.\>"; \)\), 
    \(\(Start::"\<usage\>" = "\<\>"; \)\), 
    \(\(Step::"\<usage\>" = "\<\>"; \)\), 
    \(\(Vars::"\<usage\>" = "\<\>"; \)\), 
    \(\(Begin["\<`Private`\>"]; \)\), 
    \(\((GeneratePartition[n_, v_] := {{n}} /; v \[LessEqual] 1; 
      GeneratePartition[n_, v_] := 
        Join@@Table[
              \((Prepend[#1, i]&)\)/@GeneratePartition[n - i, v - 1], {i, n, 
                0, \(-1\)}] /; v > 1; Unprotect[Power]; 0\^0 = 1; 
      \((Protect[Power]; )\))\); \n
    \((VarNames[v_] := 
        Module[{j}, 
          Table[ToExpression["\<Monomials`Private`x\>"<>ToString[j]], {j, 
              v}]]; \((
        Options[ConvertAll] = {Start \[Rule] 0, Step \[Rule] 1}; )\))\); 
    \((ConvertAll[n_, v_, opts___] := 
        \(ConvertAll[n, v, opts] = 
          Module[{homog, part, matrix, m, rhs, lhs, soln, i, j, s, h, vars}, 
            homog = GeneratePartition[n, v]; part = Rest/@homog; 
            m = Length[part]; s = \(Start /. {opts}\) /. Options[ConvertAll]; 
            h = \(Step /. {opts}\) /. Options[ConvertAll]; 
            vars = \(Vars /. {opts}\) /. {Vars \[RuleDelayed] VarNames[v]}; 
            rhs = Table[
                ToExpression["\<Monomials`private`l\>"<>ToString[j]], {j, 
                  m}]; matrix = 
              Table[Times@@
                  \(\((s + part\[LeftDoubleBracket]i\[RightDoubleBracket]\ h)
                        \)\^part\[LeftDoubleBracket]j
                        \[RightDoubleBracket]\), {i, m}, {j, m}]; 
            soln = 
              Expand[LinearSolve[matrix, rhs]\/Table[
                      Multinomial@@
                        homog\[LeftDoubleBracket]i\[RightDoubleBracket], {i, 
                        m}]] /. 
                Table[rhs\[LeftDoubleBracket]j\[RightDoubleBracket] \[Rule] 
                    \((Prepend[
                            s + part\[LeftDoubleBracket]j
                                  \[RightDoubleBracket]\ h, 1] . vars)\)\^n, {
                    j, m}]]\); 
      \((Options[Convert] = {Start \[Rule] 0, Step \[Rule] 1}; )\))\); 
    \((Convert[mon_, opts___] := 
        Module[{trueVars, coeff, n, v, expos, list, i, j, temp}, \n\t\t\t
          trueVars = Variables[mon]; \n\t\t\t
          coeff = mon /. Thread[trueVars \[Rule] 1]; \n\t\t\t
          v = Length[trueVars]; \n\t\t\t
          expos = \((Exponent[mon, #1]&)\)/@trueVars; \n\t\t\t
          n = Plus@@expos; \n\t\t\tlist = GeneratePartition[n, v]; 
          temp = \(ConvertAll[n, v, opts, Vars \[Rule] trueVars]
                \)\[LeftDoubleBracket]\(\(Position[list, expos]
                    \)\[LeftDoubleBracket]1
                  \[RightDoubleBracket]\)\[LeftDoubleBracket]1
                \[RightDoubleBracket]\[RightDoubleBracket]; 
          Plus@@\(\((coeff\ #1&)\)/@
              If[Head[temp] === Plus, List@@temp, {temp}]\)]; )\)\), 
    \(\(End[]; \)\), 
    \(\(EndPackage[]; \)\)}], "Input",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell["Here is the description of the main routine:", "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\(?Convert\)\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \("Convert[mon, Start -> s, Step -> h] expresses monomial mon of degree n \
as a linear combination of n-th powers of linear forms. The optional \
parameters affect the choice of  coefficients in these forms."\)], "Print"]
}, Closed]],

Cell["Here are some tests:", "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
    \(Convert[4\ x\ y]\), 
    \(Convert[4\ x\ y, Start \[Rule] \(-1\)]\), 
    \(Convert[4\ x\ y, Start \[Rule] \(-4\)]\)}], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\(-3\)\ x\^2 + 4\ \((x + y)\)\^2 - \((x + 2\ y)\)\^2\)], "Output"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\(-\((x - y)\)\^2\) + \((x + y)\)\^2\)], "Output"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(5\ \((x - 4\ y)\)\^2 - 12\ \((x - 3\ y)\)\^2 + 7\ \((x - 2\ y)\)\^2\)], 
  "Output"]
}, Closed]],

Cell["Here is a representation for all the cubic monomials:", "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(TableForm[
      Transpose[{Bxyz[3], \((Convert[#1, Start \[Rule] \(-1\)]&)\)/@Bxyz[3]}]]
      \)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    TagBox[GridBox[{
          {\(x\^3\), \(x\^3\)},
          {\(x\^2\ y\), 
            \(\(-\(x\^3\/6\)\) - 1\/9\ \((x - y)\)\^3 + 
              1\/3\ \((x + y)\)\^3 - 1\/18\ \((x + 2\ y)\)\^3\)},
          {\(x\ y\^2\), 
            \(\(-\(x\^3\/3\)\) + 1\/6\ \((x - y)\)\^3 + 
              1\/6\ \((x + y)\)\^3\)},
          {\(y\^3\), \(y\^3\)},
          {\(x\^2\ z\), 
            \(\(-\(x\^3\/6\)\) - 1\/9\ \((x - z)\)\^3 + 
              1\/3\ \((x + z)\)\^3 - 1\/18\ \((x + 2\ z)\)\^3\)},
          {\(x\ y\ z\), 
            \(\(-\(x\^3\/6\)\) + 1\/12\ \((x - y)\)\^3 + 
              1\/12\ \((x + y)\)\^3 + 1\/12\ \((x - z)\)\^3 - 
              1\/12\ \((x + y - z)\)\^3 + 1\/12\ \((x + z)\)\^3 - 
              1\/12\ \((x - y + z)\)\^3\)},
          {\(y\^2\ z\), 
            \(\(-\(y\^3\/6\)\) - 1\/9\ \((y - z)\)\^3 + 
              1\/3\ \((y + z)\)\^3 - 1\/18\ \((y + 2\ z)\)\^3\)},
          {\(x\ z\^2\), 
            \(\(-\(x\^3\/3\)\) + 1\/6\ \((x - z)\)\^3 + 
              1\/6\ \((x + z)\)\^3\)},
          {\(y\ z\^2\), 
            \(\(-\(y\^3\/3\)\) + 1\/6\ \((y - z)\)\^3 + 
              1\/6\ \((y + z)\)\^3\)},
          {\(z\^3\), \(z\^3\)}
          },
        RowSpacings->1,
        ColumnSpacings->3,
        RowAlignments->Baseline,
        ColumnAlignments->{Left}],
      (TableForm[ #]&)]], "Output"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[TextData[{
  "In the case of ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(x\ y\ z\)]],
  ", we see this does not give the ",
  StyleBox["shortest ",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  "representation:"
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(Expand[
      \((x - y - z)\)\^3 - \((x + y - z)\)\^3 - \((x - y + z)\)\^3 + 
        \((x + y + z)\)\^3]\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(24\ x\ y\ z\)], "Output"]
}, Closed]],

Cell["\<\
We also note the program works for polynomials in more than three \
variables (but it often gets slower):\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
    \(Convert[48\ w\ x\ y\ z]\), 
    \(Expand[%]\)}], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\(-5\)\ w\^4 + 6\ \((w + x)\)\^4 - \((w + 2\ x)\)\^4 + 
      6\ \((w + y)\)\^4 - 7\ \((w + x + y)\)\^4 + \((w + 2\ x + y)\)\^4 - 
      \((w + 2\ y)\)\^4 + \((w + x + 2\ y)\)\^4 + 6\ \((w + z)\)\^4 - 
      7\ \((w + x + z)\)\^4 + \((w + 2\ x + z)\)\^4 - 7\ \((w + y + z)\)\^4 + 
      8\ \((w + x + y + z)\)\^4 - \((w + 2\ x + y + z)\)\^4 + 
      \((w + 2\ y + z)\)\^4 - \((w + x + 2\ y + z)\)\^4 - \((w + 2\ z)\)\^4 + 
      \((w + x + 2\ z)\)\^4 + \((w + y + 2\ z)\)\^4 - 
      \((w + x + y + 2\ z)\)\^4\)], "Output"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(48\ w\ x\ y\ z\)], "Output"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
    \(Convert[240\ v\ w\ x\ y\ z]\), 
    \(Expand[%]\)}], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(6\ v\^5 - 7\ \((v + w)\)\^5 + \((v + 2\ w)\)\^5 - 7\ \((v + x)\)\^5 + 
      8\ \((v + w + x)\)\^5 - \((v + 2\ w + x)\)\^5 + \((v + 2\ x)\)\^5 - 
      \((v + w + 2\ x)\)\^5 - 7\ \((v + y)\)\^5 + 8\ \((v + w + y)\)\^5 - 
      \((v + 2\ w + y)\)\^5 + 8\ \((v + x + y)\)\^5 - 
      9\ \((v + w + x + y)\)\^5 + \((v + 2\ w + x + y)\)\^5 - 
      \((v + 2\ x + y)\)\^5 + \((v + w + 2\ x + y)\)\^5 + \((v + 2\ y)\)\^5 - 
      \((v + w + 2\ y)\)\^5 - \((v + x + 2\ y)\)\^5 + 
      \((v + w + x + 2\ y)\)\^5 - 7\ \((v + z)\)\^5 + 8\ \((v + w + z)\)\^5 - 
      \((v + 2\ w + z)\)\^5 + 8\ \((v + x + z)\)\^5 - 
      9\ \((v + w + x + z)\)\^5 + \((v + 2\ w + x + z)\)\^5 - 
      \((v + 2\ x + z)\)\^5 + \((v + w + 2\ x + z)\)\^5 + 
      8\ \((v + y + z)\)\^5 - 9\ \((v + w + y + z)\)\^5 + 
      \((v + 2\ w + y + z)\)\^5 - 9\ \((v + x + y + z)\)\^5 + 
      10\ \((v + w + x + y + z)\)\^5 - \((v + 2\ w + x + y + z)\)\^5 + 
      \((v + 2\ x + y + z)\)\^5 - \((v + w + 2\ x + y + z)\)\^5 - 
      \((v + 2\ y + z)\)\^5 + \((v + w + 2\ y + z)\)\^5 + 
      \((v + x + 2\ y + z)\)\^5 - \((v + w + x + 2\ y + z)\)\^5 + 
      \((v + 2\ z)\)\^5 - \((v + w + 2\ z)\)\^5 - \((v + x + 2\ z)\)\^5 + 
      \((v + w + x + 2\ z)\)\^5 - \((v + y + 2\ z)\)\^5 + 
      \((v + w + y + 2\ z)\)\^5 + \((v + x + y + 2\ z)\)\^5 - 
      \((v + w + x + y + 2\ z)\)\^5\)], "Output"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(240\ v\ w\ x\ y\ z\)], "Output"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[TextData[{
  "We can also convert ",
  StyleBox["polynomials",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " by just converting each term:"
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
    \(\((Convert[#1, Start \[Rule] \(-1\)]&)\)/@\((x\^3 - 4\ y\ z\^2)\)\), 
    \(Expand[%]\)}], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(x\^3 + \(4\ y\^3\)\/3 - 2\/3\ \((y - z)\)\^3 - 2\/3\ \((y + z)\)\^3\)], 
  "Output"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(x\^3 - 4\ y\ z\^2\)], "Output"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
    \(Convert/@\((x\^3 - 4\ y\ z\^2 + x\ y\ z - x\^2\ y)\)\), 
    \(Expand[%]\)}], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\(35\ x\^3\)\/18 - \(4\ y\^3\)\/3 - 17\/12\ \((x + y)\)\^3 + 
      7\/12\ \((x + 2\ y)\)\^3 - 1\/9\ \((x + 3\ y)\)\^3 - 
      5\/12\ \((x + z)\)\^3 + 10\/3\ \((y + z)\)\^3 + 
      1\/2\ \((x + y + z)\)\^3 - 1\/12\ \((x + 2\ y + z)\)\^3 + 
      1\/12\ \((x + 2\ z)\)\^3 - 8\/3\ \((y + 2\ z)\)\^3 - 
      1\/12\ \((x + y + 2\ z)\)\^3 + 2\/3\ \((y + 3\ z)\)\^3\)], "Output"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(x\^3 - x\^2\ y + x\ y\ z - 4\ y\ z\^2\)], "Output"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[TextData[{
  "We note that it should really only take ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox["10",
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  " terms at most in such a representation of a cubic, so the powers are ",
  StyleBox["not",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " independent. "
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["Question.",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "  Every homogeneous polynomial of degree ",
  StyleBox["n",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  " has a ",
  StyleBox["shortest ",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  "represention as a sum (linear combination) of ",
  StyleBox["n",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "th powers.  (We already know the upper bound on the number, but is that ",
  StyleBox["tight",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  "?)  How can the ",
  StyleBox["length",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " of such a shortest representation be found \[LongDash] and an ",
  StyleBox["example",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " of the representation as well."
}], "Text",
  Background->RGBColor[0, 1, 0]]
}, Closed]]
},
